# Foundry compendium packs are LevelDB databases. A few of their internal files
# (CURRENT, LOG, LOG.old, MANIFEST-*) are pure ASCII, so git's text detection treats
# them as text and rewrites their line endings on checkout wherever core.autocrlf is
# enabled — i.e. on most Windows clones.
#
# That is fatal for CURRENT, which must contain exactly "MANIFEST-NNNNNN\n". With a
# CRLF, LevelDB strips only the trailing \n and then looks for a file literally named
# "MANIFEST-NNNNNN\r", which cannot exist — the pack fails to open and the compendium
# is unusable. The .ldb files escape this only because they contain NUL bytes and are
# therefore auto-detected as binary.
#
# Mark the whole pack tree binary so no content filtering is ever applied to it.
packs/** binary

# Book modules ship packs of their own under modules/<id>/packs/, which are the
# same LevelDB format and need exactly the same protection.
modules/**/packs/** binary
